from datetime import date, datetime
from typing import Literal
from pydantic import BaseModel, field_validator
DATE_FORMATS = ("%d/%m/%Y", "%Y-%m-%d", "%d-%b-%y", "%d.%m.%Y")
class Patient(BaseModel):
    patient_id: str
    last_checkup: date
    mobile: str | None
    patient_type: Literal["nhs", "private"]
    @field_validator("last_checkup", mode="before")
    @classmethod
    def parse_date(cls, v):
        for fmt in DATE_FORMATS:
            try:
                return datetime.strptime(v.strip(), fmt).date()
            except ValueError:
                continue
        raise ValueError(f"unrecognized date: {v!r}")
    @field_validator("mobile", mode="before")
    @classmethod
    def normalize_mobile(cls, v):
        digits = "".join(ch for ch in (v or "") if ch.isdigit())
        if digits.startswith("07") and len(digits) == 11:
            return "+44" + digits[1:]
        return None  # unknown format: send to review queue

